{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/475860-effect-of-divorcing-blood-points-and-spirit-points","id":475860,"title":"Effect of Divorcing Blood Points and \"Spirit Points\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-10T08:43:41-07:00","id":475860,"title":"Effect of Divorcing Blood Points and \"Spirit Points\"","content":"In both VtR and VtM, more powerful vampires can store more blood, and using their powers uses up blood points and makes them thirsty. This (<a href=\"http://www.patman.org/wod/alternate/altworlds/wodannerice.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.patman.org/wod/alternate/...odannerice.asp</a>) hack divorces the two, giving Vampires a &quot;Spirit Pool&quot; which they use to power all of the powers that currently rely on blood points (except for healing and rituals), Spirit replenishes nightly.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I do this? What problems do I need to anticipate or do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:50:39-07:00","id":475887,"title":"","content":"It's a hack for Masquerade, so I'd watch out for their numbers.<br /> <br /> Firstly, not every Discipline power costs Vitae at all, so some powers will still be used frequently. If you use their numbers for Spirit however, it'll effectively leave lower BP vampires with a very limited amount of power usage per night, and you also lose one of the places where you expend the Vitae that thus necessitates hunting mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:26:59-07:00","id":475932,"title":"","content":"I remember reading that back in the day.<br /> <br /> Anyway, first thing that breaks is power stat as in there is none. You could derive one from that huge pile of spirit points but really I'd recommend making Sprit your power stat. There doesn't seem to be much gained by ranking it 1 - 1000 instead of 1 - 10. Anything that would increase or decrease spirit points in this hack instead grants or removes Spirit Beats (similar to Cover Beats but for this new Spirit power stat).<br /> <br /> The embrace, for example, would start a character off with Spirit 0 and as many Spirit Beats as their sire decided to give them. Give enough and it could equal one or more dots of Spirt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:58:56-07:00","id":475958,"title":"","content":"Nitpick - I don't know about in Masquerade, but in Requiem, vampires' various powers a fueled by Vitae, not by blood. The blood is just the vehicle, the actual resource vampires feed on and spend to activate their supernatural abilities is the life force within the blood.<br /> <br /> This seems like a much more involved hack than just replacing Vitae with spirit points. It's like a whole Anne Rice chronicle hack. It eliminates generation (which isn't a thing in Requiem), clans (which mean something very different in Requiem than they did in Masquerade) and fiddles with a lot of numbers (which are completely different in Requiem anyway). Like, the idea itself is... Something one might chose to do, though it wouldn't be to my taste... But the actual system needs a LOT of work to convert to Requiem rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:27:23-07:00","id":476131,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It's not that much to change to Requiem.</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit takes the place of Blood Potency and has it's own Spirit Exp and Spirit Beats. Max Skills and Attributes are 5 or Spirit, whichever is higher.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Maximum Power Points</b> are equal to 10 x Spirit +2 and <b>maximum Blood </b>is equal to 10 x Spirit + 10.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Blood and Power Points per round</b> are both </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">2 x Spirit + 5 per round.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Anything that adds or removes Spirit Points instead adds or removes Spirit Beats. Spirit EXP is &quot;broken down&quot; into Beats and Spirit into Spirit Exp if needed to remove enough Beats.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Everything that was removed from vampires (blood bond, ghouls, clans, ect) is the same as in the hack notes. Likewise for raising from sleep and torpor. Anything that raises difficulty instead subtracts dice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Discipline Progression, based on Spirit and Spirit Exp</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 0 - Auspex 1, Vigor 1, Majesty 1, Resilience 1, Protean 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 0, 1 Exp - Vigor 2, Resilience 2, Celerity 1, Majesty 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 0, 2 Exp - Vigor 3, Resilience 3, Celerity 2, Majesty 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 0, 3 Exp - Resilience 4, Majesty 4, PK 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 0, 4 Exp - Auspex 2, Celerity 3, Vigor 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 1 - Majesty 5, Obfuscate 2, Resilience 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 2 - Auspex 3, Majesty 6, Vigor 5, PK 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 3 - Celerity 4, Resilience 7, Obfuscate 3, Auspex 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 4 - Majesty 7, Obfuscate 4, Auspex 6, PK 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 5 - Celerity 5, Resilience 8, Obfuscate 5, Auspex 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 6 - Protean 8, Auspex 8, Obfuscate 6, Majesty 8</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 7 - Auspex 9, Obfuscate 7, Majesty 9, Resilience 9, PK 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 8 - Auspex 10, Obfuscate 8, Majesty 10</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 9 - Resilience 10, Obfuscate 9, PK 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spirit 10 - Protean 10</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I may have missed something but I think the above will be playable if this hack is to your taste. It's not a one-to-one duplicate of the percentages and numbers from before but I think it's close enough everything will run fine.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","user":"helel","date":". 04-10-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:41:28-07:00","id":476142,"title":"","content":"Omg thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T18:10:48-07:00","id":476482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/475860-effect-of-divorcing-blood-points-and-spirit-points#post475860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In both VtR and VtM, more powerful vampires can store more blood, and using their powers uses up blood points and makes them thirsty. This (<a href=\"http://www.patman.org/wod/alternate/altworlds/wodannerice.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.patman.org/wod/alternate/...odannerice.asp</a>) hack divorces the two, giving Vampires a &quot;Spirit Pool&quot; which they use to power all of the powers that currently rely on blood points (except for healing and rituals), Spirit replenishes nightly.<br /> <br /> What breaks if I do this? What problems do I need to anticipate or do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T18:14:05-07:00","id":476483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/475860-effect-of-divorcing-blood-points-and-spirit-points?p=476482#post476482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the looks of it, to emulate Anne Rice's vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T08:09:39-07:00","id":476959,"title":"","content":"For me the most important part is divorcing &quot;Magic Points&quot; from Vitae/Blood. That is, more powerful vampires have more &quot;power&quot;, but still need to hunt all the time. Unless it's literally a blood power, using your powers doesn't make you hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T08:00:30-07:00","id":477930,"title":"","content":"I thought the spirit point system emulated Anne Rice very well, especially how one gains power quickly or over time. I haven't read the hack in years, but I recall liking the spirit points, and disliking the shoehorned Disciplines. <br /> <br /> If you wanted to fit the concept into Requiem, I suppose you could do 1-100 spirit points, increased as per Wake's system, and keep blood capacity at a straight 10 points. IIRC, the need to feed decreased over the centuries; if you kept BP and advanced it at the rate given in Requiem, you could then use (11-BP) for the blood loss each night. Still doesn't directly fit with the Vampire Chronicles, but it depends on how much you want to emulate the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:44:28-07:00","id":479358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/475860-effect-of-divorcing-blood-points-and-spirit-points?p=476959#post476959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the most important part is divorcing &quot;Magic Points&quot; from Vitae/Blood. That is, more powerful vampires have more &quot;power&quot;, but still need to hunt all the time. Unless it's literally a blood power, using your powers doesn't make you hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought all vampire powers were blood powers.<br /> meh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:25:15-07:00","id":479402,"title":"","content":"Well, the current fluff is that vampires are corpses animated by dark blood-magic, so in a sense all vampire powers are magic powers as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}